- then optionally `/` followed by anything.

Nothing else may follow.

Collect the values of all URL keys, scanning the dicts in order and each dict's keys in insertion order. Return a dict with a single entry that maps the most frequent collected value to its count. On a tie, pick the value that was collected first. True and 1 (and False and 0) count as different values. If no key is a URL, return `{}`.

